# French URL redirects — added 2026-08-28.
#
# The French pages moved off the English slugs onto French ones. These rules
# keep every old link working with a real 301 (search engines and bookmarks
# follow it; the stub index.html left at each old path is only a fallback for
# the case where .htaccess is not honoured).
#
# WHY mod_alias (Redirect) AND NOT mod_rewrite: a child .htaccess that declares
# its own RewriteRule stops inheriting the parent's rewrite rules, and the
# HTTP -> HTTPS redirect for this site lives in public_html/.htaccess. Using
# Redirect here leaves that inheritance untouched.
#
# NOTE: mod_alias matches the FULL URL-path, not a path relative to this
# directory — hence the leading /fr/ on every source below.

# 2026-09-01: /fr/comment-soumettre/ merged into /fr/soumettre/, mirroring the
# English merge. Note the old /fr/how-to-apply/ rule now points straight at
# /fr/soumettre/ rather than at comment-soumettre — otherwise an old English-slug
# link would take two hops to land, and a redirect to a redirect is a thing
# search engines penalise and some clients refuse to follow.

<IfModule mod_alias.c>
Redirect 301 /fr/about-the-fund/ /fr/a-propos/
Redirect 301 /fr/how-to-apply/ /fr/soumettre/
Redirect 301 /fr/comment-soumettre/ /fr/soumettre/
Redirect 301 /fr/apply-now/ /fr/soumettre/
Redirect 301 /fr/partner-schools/ /fr/ecoles-partenaires/
Redirect 301 /fr/terms-conditions/ /fr/conditions-utilisation/
</IfModule>
